{
  "_comment": "Physical-scale testbed: one worker per physical device, no board is split into several workers. The paper's 10 devices (2 AGX + 4 NX + 4 Pi5) shrink to the 6 devices we have (1 AGX + 4 NX + 1 real Pi 5); the master runs on an NX board (orin0) as in Sec. 5.1 and keeps 2 of its cores, the co-located NX worker gets the other 6. Each worker owns all cores of its device, schedulers see the same logical CPUs. Cloud<->edge traffic is shaped to 100 Mbps (no added delay). Load is scaled with the device count (C = 4 x 6/10, rounded up to 3). TCP minimum RTO 10 ms in every node (a LAN testbed: the 200 ms default turns a burst loss into a 200 ms stall).",
